course: dictionary
lesson: 14444
title: Heart words: palpitation
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A palpitation is a feeling that your heart is beating very fast, very hard or in an uneven way. You often notice it in your chest or your neck. Most people feel palpitations only now and then. Palpitations is usually written in the plural, because people often have more than one.
explain: Read the words around the word to find its meaning. «After the fast run up the hill, Mia felt palpitations in her chest.» Running makes your heart beat faster, so palpitations must be about a racing heart. Ask yourself: does my meaning make sense in the sentence?
explain: Grown-ups sometimes joke about palpitations. «You nearly gave me palpitations when you jumped out!» Here the word does not mean a real heart problem. It means you gave a big fright and made the speaker's heart race with shock.
fact: A palpitation means your heart feels like it is beating very fast, very hard or unevenly.
fact: Palpitations can happen when you are very scared, when you exercise, after too much caffeine, or when you are ill.
fact: If palpitations keep happening, you should tell a grown-up and see a doctor.
fact: In a joke, «You gave me palpitations!» means you gave someone a big fright or a lot of nervous excitement.
exercise: «After the fast run up the hill, Mia felt palpitations in her chest.» What are palpitations? | A loud sneeze that comes without warning | A sore feeling in your legs after walking | A small cut on your finger | *A feeling that your heart is beating very fast or unevenly
exercise: «You nearly gave me palpitations when you jumped out!» What does the speaker mean? | You have a loud voice | You are a very good dancer | You made me feel very sleepy | *You gave me a big fright
exercise: Which of these can cause palpitations? | Reading a book quietly | Drawing a picture of a tree | Being very scared | *Being very scared, or exercising hard
exercise: Lily says, «My heart was racing all night, so I had palpitations.» Which sentence is best? | Lily was happy and went to sleep fast | *Lily's heart was beating fast and unevenly, and she should tell a grown-up | Lily's heart was made of gold | Lily had a cold and a runny nose
test: «Tom had palpitations after the race, so his coach told him to rest.» What does palpitations mean? | A long rest in bed | A sore muscle in the arm | A type of race for young runners | *A fast, hard or uneven heartbeat
test: «If your palpitations keep coming back, see a doctor.» Why should you see a doctor? | Because a doctor is always needed for a cold | Because palpitations always mean you are happy | *Because the palpitations keep happening | Because doctors give out sweets
exam: «Ali's heart did palpitations in the dark, and he said, "You gave me palpitations, Mum!"» | Palpitations means a sleepy yawn | Palpitations means a small toy | The palpitations are a kind of dance | *The palpitations are about a fast or uneven heartbeat, and the joke means a big fright
